(assertion-shape: not a claim row - the two assertion shapes every
 assertable row in this ledger names, proven to compile and to reach
 exit 95. Kept because OPR-40 makes the obvious shape illegal: a
 comparison is not a first-class expression, so a comparison row cannot
 assert `If <comparison> is not true`. It has to route through a
 witness variable instead, which is the second half of this file.
 Arithmetic and bitwise rows have no such problem and use the first
 half.
 Proven by hand once in each direction: changing the 26 on line 3 to 99
 makes this program print `ASSERT OPR-01: expected 99` and exit 95,
 and changing the 1 on line 8 to 0 makes it print the OPR-15 line and
 exit 95. Both were run; neither is left in the file, so the recorded
 output below is the passing one.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox assertion-shape.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   value assertion passed
   witness assertion passed
)
(Shape one - arithmetic and bitwise rows assert the value directly.)
a number called lhs is 20.
a number called rhs is 6.
If lhs add rhs is not 26 then, Print "ASSERT OPR-01: expected 26", Exit 95.
Print "value assertion passed".

(Shape two - comparison and logical rows route through a witness.)
a number called witness is 0.
If lhs is greater than rhs then, Set witness to 1.
If witness is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT OPR-15: expected greater-than to fire", Exit 95.
Print "witness assertion passed".
